  "notes": "Manuscript page 8, pencil 16. The author describes enlarging the Teichmüller–Poincaré groupoid to a category linking numerical types, then states his “programme à l’horizon”: determine the Galois–Teichmüller category together with field-automorphism operations, especially for the algebraic closure of Q and algebraic closures of finitely generated fields. His insertion specifies an “algébrique” route, neither transcendental nor algebraic-geometric; the margin explains this through surface topology, combinatorics (“cartes”), and profinite group theory. The source grammar “des courbes alg. relatifs” and “topologie surfaces” is retained. The last sign is (?) with a visible dot, not an additional Q condition. The alphabet of the isolated Q after type fini sur remains uncertain.",
